print(f"Average percentage error: {mape:.1f}%")

# RMSE as % of mean
rmse_percent = (np.sqrt(mse) / np.mean(y_test)) * 100
print(f"RMSE as % of mean: {rmse_percent:.1f}%")
```

**Key Points:**
🔑 R²: Primary metric for explaining variance
🔑 RMSE: Interpretable, same units as target
🔑 MAE: Robust to outliers
🔑 Adjusted R²: Fair model comparison
🔑 Always use holdout/cross-validation test set
🔑 Compare train vs test error (check overfitting)

