Feature interactions: Implicit
```

**Linear Models (Linear/Logistic Regression):**
```
Model type: Parametric, linear
Decision boundary: Linear hyperplane
Interpretability: Very high (coefficients)
Training: Very fast
Prediction: Very fast (dot product)
Feature scaling: Often needed
Feature interactions: Must engineer manually
```

**Head-to-Head Comparison:**

```
Aspect                | Decision Tree | Linear Model
Nonlinear patterns    | ✓ Automatic  | ✗ Needs features
Interpretability      | ✓ Rules      | ✓ Coefficients
Computation           | Medium       | Very fast
Feature engineering   | ✗ Not needed | ✓ Usually needed
Overfitting risk      | High         | Low
Categorical features  | ✓ Direct     | ✗ Must encode
Missing data          | ✗ Can't use  | ✓ Can impute
Extrapolation         | ✗ Constant   | ✓ Continues
Stability             | Low          | High
```

**When to Use Decision Trees:**

```
✓ Nonlinear relationships needed
✓ Categorical features present
✓ Feature importance critical
✓ Simple rules important ("If X > 5, then...")
✓ Relatively small datasets
✓ Mixed feature types
✓ No feature scaling possible

Example applications:
- Medical diagnosis (interpretable rules)
- Credit decisions (regulatory requirements)
- Customer segmentation
- Fraud detection with explainability
```

**When to Use Linear Models:**

```
