## 📌 Introduction to Ensemble Methods

**Why Ensemble Methods?**
Single model has limitations. Combining multiple models often better.

**Types of Ensemble:**
```
Voting: Multiple models, average predictions
Bagging: Multiple models trained on different data subsets
Boosting: Sequential models, each corrects previous
Stacking: Multiple models, meta-model learns to combine
```

**Wisdom of Crowds Analogy:**
```
Single expert opinion: May be biased
Average of many experts: Often better
Key: Experts must disagree in useful ways
```

**Random Forest:**
```
- Ensemble of decision trees
- Each tree trained on different data sample
- Predictions averaged (regression) or voted (classification)
- Reduces variance, controls overfitting
```

