plt.show()
```

**When to Use Hard Margin:**

```
✓ Data provably separable
✓ No outliers present
✓ All points on correct side critical
✓ Small datasets with clean labels

In practice: Rarely used (hard to achieve perfect separation)
```

**When to Use Soft Margin:**

```
✓ Real-world data with noise
✓ Outliers present
✓ Noise in labels
✓ Want robustness

In practice: Almost always (default choice)
```

**C Parameter Selection:**

```
Large C (→∞): Hard margin behavior
- Minimize violations (fit training noise)
- Risk: Overfitting
- Wide margin reduced to fit outliers

Small C: Soft margin behavior
- Tolerates more violations
- Risk: Underfitting
- Wider margin, better generalization

Optimal C: Cross-validation to find best trade-off
```

**Code - C Selection via Cross-Validation:**
