## ⚖️ Comparison with Other Methods

### K-Means vs Hierarchical Clustering

```
K-Means:
✓ Fast (O(nk))
✓ Scalable to large datasets
✓ Specify k upfront
✗ Hard assignments (point in one cluster)
✗ Globular clusters only
✗ Sensitive to initialization

Hierarchical:
✓ No need to specify k upfront
✓ Can cut dendrogram at any level
✓ Any shape clusters (agglomerative variant)
✓ More interpretable
✗ O(n²) memory, O(n² log n) time
✗ Slower
✗ Can't undo merges
```

### K-Means vs DBSCAN

```
K-Means:
✓ Simple, fast
✓ Works with any distance metric
✓ Probabilistic interpretation (EM algorithm)
✓ Handles outliers via soft assignment
✗ Must know k
✗ Assumes globular clusters
✗ Sensitive to scale

DBSCAN:
✓ No need for k
✓ Arbitrary cluster shapes
✓ Handles outliers (labels as noise)
✓ Density-based (realistic)
✗ Slower O(n log n) with KDTree
✗ Sensitive to ε and min_pts parameters
✗ Difficult with varying density
```

