## ✅ Advantages & Limitations

**Advantages:**
```
✓ Fast and efficient (linear in n, k, d, i)
✓ Easily parallelizable
✓ Works well with large datasets
✓ Scales to high dimensions
✓ Simple to implement and understand
✓ Soft K-Means gives probabilities
```

**Limitations:**
```
✗ Must specify k in advance
✗ Sensitive to initialization
✗ Assumes roughly equal cluster sizes
✗ Sensitive to outliers (hard assignment)
✗ Assumes globular (spherical) clusters
✗ Converges to local optimum
✗ Normalized features important (euclidean distance)
