## 📌 Introduction & Intuition

**What is Naive Bayes?**
Probabilistic classifier based on Bayes' theorem with conditional independence assumption.

```
Goal: Find P(class | features)
      Probability of class given features

Bayes Theorem:
P(class | features) = P(features | class) × P(class) / P(features)

Naive Assumption:
Features independent given class
P(f₁, f₂, ... | class) = P(f₁|class) × P(f₂|class) × ...
```

**Key Idea:**
```
1. Assume features are independent (naive assumption)
2. Learn class-conditional distributions P(feature|class)
3. Use Bayes theorem to classify new points
4. Posterior ∝ likelihood × prior
```

**When to Use:**
- Text classification (spam detection, sentiment analysis)
- Document categorization
- Email filtering
- Fast training needed
- High-dimensional data
- Categorical/discrete features

